  "note": "Three upturned roofs, dark timber bracing and a gilt finial identify the whitewashed shrine. An open cross-gabled entry pavilion links the stepped bathing terraces and the upper spring court. Street and close-up geometry includes all 108 spouts. Standard Terrarium samples set the foundations and the landings on three separate terraces. Authored basin water and the spring wall replace native water within their mapped bounds. The surrounding terrain, independent buildings and transportation remain host data. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
